// Title: Sysinternals PsSuspend Execution
// Sigma ID: 48bbc537-b652-4b4e-bd1d-281172df448f
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-03-23 | Modified: 2026-06-29
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, discovery, persistence, T1543.003
// Description: Detects usage of Sysinternals PsSuspend which can be abused to suspend critical processes
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/pssuspend
//   - https://twitter.com/0gtweet/status/1638069413717975046
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_sysinternals_pssuspend_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "pssuspend.exe" or (FolderPath endswith "\\pssuspend.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pssuspend64.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pssuspend64a.exe")
